      "kind": "grammar",
      "title": "broren min, søstera mi",
      "text": "The little word for \"my\" comes after the noun and changes a little with it: broren min (a masculine word), søstera mi (a feminine word). The endings -en and -a on the noun itself mean \"the\": broren is \"the brother\", søstera is \"the sister\". So \"broren min\" is literally \"the brother my\". Notice too that nouns start with a small letter in Norwegian: broren, søstera.",
